course: dictionary
lesson: 5259
title: A sudden shake: jolt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A jolt is a sudden, hard shake or bump. It can also be a sudden shock. Look at the clues around the word: «The bus stopped with a jolt» tells you the bus stopped suddenly and everyone was shaken, so a jolt is a sudden shake.
explain: Jolt can also be a verb, an action word. «The alarm jolted me awake» means the alarm shook me into waking up suddenly. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is it something being done?
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence: «The news gave me a jolt» becomes «The news gave me a sudden shock». It still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Jolt as a noun means a sudden hard shake or bump, or a sudden shock.
fact: Jolt as a verb means to move or shake suddenly and roughly, or to shock someone into action.
fact: «With a jolt» and «jolt awake» are common phrases.
fact: In science, a jolt can shake your body, so seatbelts protect you from the jolt when a vehicle stops suddenly.
fact: «Concussion» is a brain injury caused by a jolt that shakes the brain inside the skull.
exercise: «The bus stopped with a jolt, and everyone grabbed a seat.» What is a jolt here? | A loud horn | A slow, gentle stop | A bus ticket | *A sudden hard shake or bump
exercise: «The news gave me a jolt.» Which phrase means the same as a jolt here? | Laughed out loud | Went to sleep | A long walk | *A sudden shock
exercise: Which word in «The alarm jolted me awake» is a verb? | *jolted | awake | alarm | me
test: «We do not feel the spin because it is perfectly smooth; you only feel motion when it speeds up, slows down or jolts.» What does jolts mean here? | *Moves or shakes suddenly and roughly | Floats gently | Stays perfectly still | Sings loudly
test: Why do seatbelts protect you from a jolt? | They make the vehicle go faster | They help the driver sing | They keep the car warm | *They stop your body from being thrown forward when a vehicle stops suddenly
exam: «Rocks along a fault strain for years until suddenly they slip, and the jolt shakes the ground: that is an earthquake.» What is the jolt in this sentence? | *The sudden shake when the rocks slip | A long quiet night | A slow drift of the rocks | A cloud of dust
